    "title": "Spring freeze to hit early next week for northeastern and central Pennsylvania - NewsBreak",
    "text": "4 hours ago PENNSYLVANIA, USA — For the second day in a row, northeastern and central Pennsylvania got a taste of summertime as temperatures topped out above 80 degrees. The spring warm-up will be short-lived. The average high so far this spring in the Scranton area is 57. The average low is 35. That is 6 degrees above average and the 4th warmest spring since 1950. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
